---
/**
 * The logo: a framed cell, solid on the left and hatched on the right.
 *
 * It is the site's own measurement grammar at its smallest — every meter here
 * draws what was measured solid and what was NOT measured hatched, never as a
 * zero — so the mark says what the product does before a word is read. One
 * colour pair only: `--signal` fills, `--signal-ink` draws the frame and hatch,
 * which is what keeps it visible on the lit-slate light theme, where a bare
 * amber fill is 1.39:1 (`tokens.css`).
 *
 * The hatch is explicit strokes under a clip rather than the meters'
 * `<pattern>`: at 16–30px a pattern's phase lands anywhere, and three drawn
 * strokes stay crisp. SVG attributes cannot read CSS custom properties, so
 * every colour arrives through a class (`site-header.css`).
 */
---

<a class="wordmark" href="/">
  <svg class="wordmark__mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <defs>
      <clipPath id="wordmark-void">
        <rect x="13.5" y="2.5" width="8" height="19"></rect>
      </clipPath>
    </defs>
    <rect class="wordmark__measured" x="2.5" y="2.5" width="11" height="19"></rect>
    <g clip-path="url(#wordmark-void)">
      <path class="wordmark__hatch" d="M10 26 L27 9 M10 21 L27 4 M10 31 L27 14 M10 16 L27 -1"></path>
    </g>
    <rect class="wordmark__frame" x="1.5" y="1.5" width="21" height="21" rx="2.5"></rect>
  </svg>
  <span>mcpwatchman</span>
</a>
